43 #edb/ref 17592186173004 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172189 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172189 #edb/ref 1045 "Affine Transformations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172189 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186173004 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172189 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049012 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172189 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "81efeb5d-b89e-5c14-80c7-9be44b7d6319" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173001 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186173003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173001 #edb/ref 1061 35594 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173001 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0a350174-3107-5bfc-b7cf-86f7ef4d3531" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173001 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186172092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173002 #edb/ref 1061 35595 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173002 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7d8f185d-3b89-591e-8ca2-fdba1ecfbeff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173002 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186172093 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173003 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186173002 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173003 #edb/ref 1061 35598 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173003 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "27929e1f-7191-5a61-bf7e-56af8100e9f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173003 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186172094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173004 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186173001 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173004 #edb/ref 1061 35599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173004 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d639fa1f-d747-5b31-9f98-2bdd4bf28119" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173004 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186173206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173206 #edb/ref 1064 "An **affine transformation** $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function that can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nUnder this notation, \n\n- $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]$ represents vectors belonging to the input space, and\n\n- $[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]$  represents vectors belonging to the output space.\n\nFor example,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis an affine transformation because it can be expressed in the form $\\mathbf x = A\\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v+1 \\\\ 2u+v-3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v \\\\ 2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the transformation\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis not affine since it contains the quadratic term $uv.$\n\nFinally, note the following relationships between affine and linear transformations:\n\n- A linear transformation $\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u$ is a special case of an affine transformation with $\\mathbf b = \\mathbf 0.$\n\n- For an affine transformation $\\mathbf T$ given by $\\mathbf x = A\\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,$ we say that $A$ is *the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with* $\\mathbf T.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173206 #edb/ref 1065 5808 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173206 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "4b154eb4-94cc-5d7b-8120-56085be85703" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173206 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247480 #edb/ref 1080 "8\\sqrt{8}\\,\\text{arcsec}(x)+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247480 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247480 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "06349d8e-8391-574b-b6ee-d09717af159e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247786 #edb/ref 1080 "8\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{8}x)+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247786 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247786 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "28b08c9d-77c7-5bea-8de3-24e47c4a6b22" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248097 #edb/ref 1080 "\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{8}x)+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248097 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248097 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4b4c8ae4-b8b1-5ed2-b232-73c90f37ed26" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248778 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{8}\\,\\text{arcsec}(x)+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248778 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248778 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "97ffb8aa-ac92-5db2-a3d4-4a6b34576f59" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249084 #edb/ref 1080 "8\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{8}})+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249084 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249084 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b9b1dd01-2ffe-53eb-9456-1dfad676593b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250090 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186247480 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250090 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186247786 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250090 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186248097 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250090 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186248778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250090 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186249084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250090 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250090 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250090 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186247786 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250090 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f124bfeb-924c-5974-b5d6-5bac9d8b7458" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250178 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186250090 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250178 #edb/ref 1069 "q-114056" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250178 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250178 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{8}{|x|\\sqrt{8{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250178 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d978df6a-8484-5ed1-885e-b4758185514d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250178 #edb/ref 1074 "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{8}{|x|\\sqrt{8{x}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{8\\sqrt{8}}{|\\sqrt{8}x|\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{8}x)^{2}-1}}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $\\sqrt{8}x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\sqrt{8}x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{8}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8}{|x|\\sqrt{8{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{8\\sqrt{8}}{|\\sqrt{8}x|\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{8}x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{8}\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{8}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =8\\,\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =8\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{8}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272960 #edb/ref 1080 "200" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272960 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272960 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "429fc6d3-040f-5f6d-9562-a7483a6f7e50" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186273651 #edb/ref 1080 "160" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186273651 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186273651 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "915bd91d-510a-52c4-8eda-cace36b4483c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186273677 #edb/ref 1080 "140" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186273677 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186273677 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "944ddaaf-6718-5e13-8c8a-dfc92fe0837b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186273749 #edb/ref 1080 "150" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186273749 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186273749 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9dcdc226-b480-5014-a556-e5f26733ab54" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274000 #edb/ref 1080 "180" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274000 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274000 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b99838c4-4a0a-5c0c-9aef-ec1151de3c3a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274974 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186272960 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274974 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186273651 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274974 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186273677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274974 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186273749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274974 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186274000 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274974 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274974 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274974 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186273749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274974 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c248cc1a-247a-52fe-80b9-786545ae3c63" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275237 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186274974 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275237 #edb/ref 1069 "q-149717" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275237 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275237 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}({a}_{i}+1)({b}_{j}-1)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{a}_{i}=20,\\,{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}{b}_{j}=26.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275237 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c995cbf9-c89f-5f4e-b314-1e2fc502c516" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275237 #edb/ref 1074 "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{b}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}({a}_{i}+1)({b}_{j}-1) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}({a}_{i}+1){\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}({b}_{j}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}({a}_{i}+1){\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}({b}_{j}-1) & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{a}_{i}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}1)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}{b}_{j}-{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}1) \\\\  & =(20+5)\\cdot (26-20) \\\\  & =(25)\\cdot (6) \\\\  & =150.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302688 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302688 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302688 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2459a5ff-007e-530b-8edd-f46a552247c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303014 #edb/ref 1080 "I, II, and III" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303014 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303014 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5b4a8220-7054-525a-8afa-9194364f34cf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303299 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303299 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303299 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "86c7d469-f99c-5c11-aeb9-bf421146bc71" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303364 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303364 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303364 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "923a9172-9e8c-54b3-b41b-41a15e5952e6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303958 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303958 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303958 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "efe9d738-6b6f-52a9-a41b-35b9bd06d1fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304611 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186302688 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304611 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186303014 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304611 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186303299 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304611 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186303364 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304611 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186303958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304611 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304611 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304611 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186302688 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304611 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c46c2ddf-b5c1-516e-be0e-d85055c76fbb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304939 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304611 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304939 #edb/ref 1069 "q-331729" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304939 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304939 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following first-order linear differential equations are homogeneous?\n\n- ${y}^{′}+7xy=5$\n- ${y}^{′}+7xy=0$\n- ${y}^{′}+7xy=-2y$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304939 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f8cfe21c-18ac-5f6d-9859-3a5cbe483542" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304939 #edb/ref 1074 "A first-order linear differential equation is homogeneous if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each equation in turn.\n\n- First, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+7xy=5.\n$$\n\nThe presence of the constant term $5$ means the right-hand side is not zero, and so it cannot be rewritten in homogeneous form. Thus, this equation is *not* homogeneous.\n\n- Next, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+7xy=0.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is already zero, so the equation directly matches the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\n- Finally, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+7xy=-2y.\n$$\n\nWe move the term involving $y$ to the left side so that all $y$-terms are together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+7xy & =-2y \\\\ {y}^{′}+7xy+2y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{′}+(7x+2)y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis matches the homogeneous form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$  Therefore, this equation *is* homogeneous.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355333 #edb/ref 1080 "$Q$ and $R$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355333 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355333 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4aed7340-5f0e-5165-ab13-314353711b81" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355880 #edb/ref 1080 "$Q$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355880 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355880 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8963ef11-348f-5e5f-8b9b-9f406cee908f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356004 #edb/ref 1080 "$P$ and $Q$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356004 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356004 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "97fba95d-9f14-57b0-a978-2376e948fa78" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
